caption: Base Cost
technology-rule: base-cost

Let:

D = Design Point Load.

M = margin of success on the successful Prototype roll.

R_C = Cost Refinement.

The Cost Factor is a percentage of baseline cost.

If R_C = 0:

Cost Factor = max(25, 100 - M)

If R_C >= 1:

Cost Floor = max(5, 25 - 5 * R_C)

Cost Factor = max(Cost Floor, 100 - 5 * R_C * M)

Normal Market Cost (normal or cinematic) = D * Cost Factor / 100

Normal Market Cost (supernatural) = D * Cost Factor

Production Cost = Normal Market Cost / 2

Production Cost = D * Cost Factor / 200

At a Cost Factor of 100, Normal Market Cost is $1 per DPL and Production Cost is $0.50 per DPL.

Round final Normal Market Cost and Production Cost to the nearest cent unless the campaign uses a coarser currency unit. Use the second, higher Normal Market Cost for any chem where any of the traits have an Origin other than Cinematic.
